cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this schema, the annotation corpus, or the mapping tooling,
  please cite this repository. A manuscript describing the model (extended
  version for arXiv, condensed version under journal submission) is in
  preparation; this file will be updated with the preferred citation when
  it is available.
title: "Forome Genetic Evidence Model (GEM)"
version: 0.2.5
date-released: 2026-09-03
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22260686
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22260686
    description: Concept DOI (resolves to the latest release)
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22260773
    description: Version DOI for v0.2.2
abstract: >
  A semantic model for scientific and genetic evidence from the biomedical
  literature, designed to support variant interpretation and AI-ready
  clinical infrastructure. The repository provides the schema (SHACL
  shapes), an annotation corpus of six publications spanning human,
  population, model-organism and polygenic-score genetics, the extraction
  pipeline that transforms PDF-level annotations into structured YAML, a
  curated term-level UMLS crosswalk of the dimensional vocabulary, and the
  GEM Mapping Studio, a standalone curation tool for defining mapping axes
  and adjudicating value-level mappings.
